        {
          "comments": "NOT REVIEWED — raw running config supplied for manual review; no automated pass, finding, or applicability decision asserted.",
          "finding_details": "Raw running config SHA-256: 14e32fd444871f594a733bad16f6c9998b6eeb7de6fa2a9254faaedefde040c5\nOfficial Cisco benchmark SHA-256: f6197e93ca098791202702bc104d88200c882e7d1c95e1a61e883c8ef042d3e3\nRunning config alone does not verify this control's complete operational check; manual review required.",
          "fix_text": "Configure the external and internal ACLs to drop all fragmented ICMP packets destined to itself as shown in the example below:\n\nSW1(config)# ip access-list EXTERNAL_ACL\nSW1(config-acl)# 35 deny icmp any host x.11.1.2 fragments log\nSW1(config-acl)# exit\n\nSW1(config)# ip access-list INTERNAL_ACL\nSW1(config-acl)# 25 deny icmp any host 10.1.12.2 fragments log\nSW1(config-acl)# end\n\nNote: Ensure the above statement is before any permit statements for ICMP.",
          "group_id": "V-221081",
          "group_id_src": "V-221081",
          "group_title": "SRG-NET-000205-RTR-000002",
          "rule_id": "SV-221081r999690_rule",
          "rule_id_src": "SV-221081r999690_rule",
          "rule_title": "The Cisco switch must be configured to drop all fragmented Internet Control Message Protocol (ICMP) packets destined to itself.",
