        {
          "comments": "NOT REVIEWED — raw running config supplied for manual review; no automated pass, finding, or applicability decision asserted.",
          "finding_details": "Raw running config SHA-256: 14e32fd444871f594a733bad16f6c9998b6eeb7de6fa2a9254faaedefde040c5\nOfficial Cisco benchmark SHA-256: f6197e93ca098791202702bc104d88200c882e7d1c95e1a61e883c8ef042d3e3\nRunning config alone does not verify this control's complete operational check; manual review required.",
          "fix_text": "Step 1: Configure an inbound ACL to deny all other traffic by default as shown in the example below:\n\nSW1(config)# ip access-list EXTERNAL_ACL\nSW1(config-acl)# permit tcp host x.11.1.1 eq bgp host x.11.1.2 \nSW1(config-acl)# permit tcp host x.11.1.1 host x.11.1.2 eq bgp\nSW1(config-acl)# permit icmp host x.11.1.1 host x.11.1.2 echo\nSW1(config-acl)# permit icmp host x.11.1.1 host x.11.1.2 echo-reply\nSW1(config-acl)# permit tcp any x.11.2.3/32 eq www\nSW1(config-acl)# permit …\n…\n…\n…\nSW1(config-acl)# deny ip any any log\n\nStep 2: Apply the ingress filter to all external interfaces.\n\nSW1(config)#int e1/2\nSW1(config-if)#ip access-group EXTERNAL_ACL in",
          "group_id": "V-221087",
          "group_id_src": "V-221087",
          "group_title": "SRG-NET-000202-RTR-000001",
          "rule_id": "SV-221087r1137935_rule",
          "rule_id_src": "SV-221087r1137935_rule",
          "rule_title": "The Cisco perimeter switch must be configured to deny network traffic by default and allow network traffic by exception.",
          "rule_version": "CISC-RT-000240",
          "severity": "high",
          "status": "not_reviewed",
          "stig_uuid": "596feb4a-431e-570b-a662-0c09ecde0742",
          "uuid": "f14b64c6-2568-5986-8253-c1370425e7b2",
          "weight": "10.0"
