          "uuid": "ce8b524b-e234-5b24-9b71-134eed50fe7f",
          "weight": "10.0"
        },
        {
          "comments": "NOT REVIEWED — raw running config supplied for manual review; no automated pass, finding, or applicability decision asserted.",
          "finding_details": "Raw running config SHA-256: 14e32fd444871f594a733bad16f6c9998b6eeb7de6fa2a9254faaedefde040c5\nOfficial Cisco benchmark SHA-256: f6197e93ca098791202702bc104d88200c882e7d1c95e1a61e883c8ef042d3e3\nRunning config alone does not verify this control's complete operational check; manual review required.",
          "fix_text": "Configure the switch to use an inbound ACL on all external interfaces as shown in the example below to restrict traffic in accordance with the guidelines contained in DOD Instruction 8551.1.\n\nSW2(config)# ip access-list EXTERNAL_ACL\nSW2(config-acl)# permit tcp any any established\nSW2(config-acl)# permit tcp x.11.1.1/32 eq bgp x.11.1.2/32 \nSW2(config-acl)# permit tcp x.11.1.1/32 x.11.1.2/32 eq bgp \nSW2(config-acl)# permit icmp x.11.1.1/32 x.11.1.2/32 echo \nSW2(config-acl)# permit icmp x.11.1.1/32 x.11.1.2/32 echo-reply \nSW2(config-acl)# permit tcp any x.11.2.3/32 eq www \n…\n… \u003c must be in accordance with DoD Instruction 8551.1\u003e\n…\nSW2(config-acl)# deny ip any any log\nSW2(config-acl)# exit\nSW1(config)#int e2/2\nSW1(config-if)# ip access-group EXTERNAL_ACL in\nSW1(config-if)# end",
          "group_id": "V-221092",
          "group_id_src": "V-221092",
          "group_title": "SRG-NET-000205-RTR-000003",
