        {
          "comments": "NOT REVIEWED — raw running config supplied for manual review; no automated pass, finding, or applicability decision asserted.",
          "finding_details": "Raw running config SHA-256: 14e32fd444871f594a733bad16f6c9998b6eeb7de6fa2a9254faaedefde040c5\nOfficial Cisco benchmark SHA-256: f6197e93ca098791202702bc104d88200c882e7d1c95e1a61e883c8ef042d3e3\nRunning config alone does not verify this control's complete operational check; manual review required.",
          "fix_text": "Configure the switch to rate limit RSVP messages per interface as shown in the example below. Configure the MPLS switch to synchronize IGP and LDP, minimizing packet loss when an IGP adjacency is established prior to LDP peers completing label exchange.\n\nOSPF Example\n\nSW1(config)# router ospf 1\nSW1(config-switch)# mpls ldp sync\n\nIS-IS Example\n\nSW1(config)# router isis\nSW1(config-switch)# mpls ldp sync.\n\nSW1(config)# ip rsvp\nSW1(config-ip-rsvp)# signaling refresh reduction \nSW1(config-ip-rsvp)# end",
          "group_id": "V-221115",
          "group_id_src": "V-221115",
          "group_title": "SRG-NET-000193-RTR-000001",
          "rule_id": "SV-221115r999724_rule",
          "rule_id_src": "SV-221115r999724_rule",
          "rule_title": "The MPLS switch with RSVP-TE enabled must be configured with message pacing to adjust maximum burst and maximum number of RSVP messages to an output queue based on the link speed and input queue size of adjacent core switches.",
          "rule_version": "CISC-RT-000610",
          "severity": "low",
          "status": "not_reviewed",
