        {
          "comments": "NOT REVIEWED — raw running config supplied for manual review; no automated pass, finding, or applicability decision asserted.",
          "finding_details": "Raw running config SHA-256: 14e32fd444871f594a733bad16f6c9998b6eeb7de6fa2a9254faaedefde040c5\nOfficial Cisco benchmark SHA-256: f6197e93ca098791202702bc104d88200c882e7d1c95e1a61e883c8ef042d3e3\nRunning config alone does not verify this control's complete operational check; manual review required.",
          "fix_text": "Configure neighbor prefix lists to only accept PIM control plane traffic from documented PIM neighbors. \n\nStep 1: Configure prefix list for each PIM neighbor.\n\nSW1(config)# ip prefix-list PIM_NEIGHBOR seq 5 permit 10.1.12.2/32\nSW1(config)# ip prefix-list PIM_NEIGHBOR deny 0.0.0.0/0 le 32\n\nStep 2: Apply a prefix to all interfaces enabled for PIM.\n\nSW1(config)# int e2/1\nSW1(config-if)# ip pim neighbor-policy prefix-list PIM_NEIGHBOR \nSW1(config-if)# end",
          "group_id": "V-221133",
          "group_id_src": "V-221133",
          "group_title": "SRG-NET-000019-RTR-000004",
          "rule_id": "SV-221133r1137911_rule",
