        {
          "comments": "NOT REVIEWED — raw running config supplied for manual review; no automated pass, finding, or applicability decision asserted.",
          "finding_details": "Raw running config SHA-256: 14e32fd444871f594a733bad16f6c9998b6eeb7de6fa2a9254faaedefde040c5\nOfficial Cisco benchmark SHA-256: f6197e93ca098791202702bc104d88200c882e7d1c95e1a61e883c8ef042d3e3\nRunning config alone does not verify this control's complete operational check; manual review required.",
          "fix_text": "Configure the DR on a global or interface basis to limit the number of mroute states resulting from IGMP or MLD membership reports.\n\nSW1(config)# int e2/4\nSW1(config-if)# ip igmp state-limit 44 \nSW1(config-if)# end",
          "group_id": "V-221140",
          "group_id_src": "V-221140",
          "group_title": "SRG-NET-000362-RTR-000122",
          "rule_id": "SV-221140r999749_rule",
          "rule_id_src": "SV-221140r999749_rule",
          "rule_title": "The Cisco multicast Designated switch (DR) must be configured to limit the number of mroute states resulting from Internet Group Management Protocol (IGMP) and Multicast Listener Discovery (MLD) Host Membership Reports.",
          "rule_version": "CISC-RT-000880",
          "severity": "medium",
          "status": "not_reviewed",
          "stig_uuid": "596feb4a-431e-570b-a662-0c09ecde0742",
          "uuid": "9c9d25a8-5bb3-55e1-893d-f5eb30758d69",
          "weight": "10.0"
        },
        {
          "comments": "NOT REVIEWED — raw running config supplied for manual review; no automated pass, finding, or applicability decision asserted.",
          "finding_details": "Raw running config SHA-256: 14e32fd444871f594a733bad16f6c9998b6eeb7de6fa2a9254faaedefde040c5\nOfficial Cisco benchmark SHA-256: f6197e93ca098791202702bc104d88200c882e7d1c95e1a61e883c8ef042d3e3\nRunning config alone does not verify this control's complete operational check; manual review required.",
          "fix_text": "Configure the DR to increase the SPT threshold or set it to infinity to minimalize (S, G) state within the multicast topology where ASM is deployed.\n\nStep 1: Configure a prefix list or route map to specify the ASM groups. The example below includes all global ASM groups.\n\nSW1(config)# ip prefix-list SPT_GROUPS permit 233.0.0.0/8\n\nStep 2. Configure the SPT threshold to infinity.\n\nSW1(config)# ip pim spt-threshold infinity group prefix-list SPT_GROUPS \nSW1(config)# end",
          "group_id": "V-221141",
          "group_id_src": "V-221141",
          "group_title": "SRG-NET-000362-RTR-000123",
          "rule_id": "SV-221141r999750_rule",
          "rule_id_src": "SV-221141r999750_rule",
          "rule_title": "The Cisco multicast Designated switch (DR) must be configured to set the shortest-path tree (SPT) threshold to infinity to minimalize source-group (S, G) state within the multicast topology where Any Source Multicast (ASM) is deployed.",
          "rule_version": "CISC-RT-000890",
          "severity": "medium",
          "status": "not_reviewed",
          "stig_uuid": "596feb4a-431e-570b-a662-0c09ecde0742",
          "uuid": "9ee921dd-12ba-56fc-978d-e87533dfafef",
          "weight": "10.0"
        },
        {
          "comments": "NOT REVIEWED — raw running config supplied for manual review; no automated pass, finding, or applicability decision asserted.",
          "finding_details": "Raw running config SHA-256: 14e32fd444871f594a733bad16f6c9998b6eeb7de6fa2a9254faaedefde040c5\nOfficial Cisco benchmark SHA-256: f6197e93ca098791202702bc104d88200c882e7d1c95e1a61e883c8ef042d3e3\nRunning config alone does not verify this control's complete operational check; manual review required.",
          "fix_text": "Configure the receive path or interface ACLs to only accept MSDP packets from known MSDP peers.\n\nSW1(config)# ip access-list EXTERNAL_ACL_INBOUND\nSW1(config-acl) # permit tcp any any established\nSW1(config-acl) # permit tcp host x.1.28.2 host x.1.28.8 eq 639\nSW1(config-acl) # deny tcp any host x1.28.8 eq 639\nSW1(config-acl) # permit tcp host x.1.28.2 host x.1.28.8 eq bgp\nSW1(config-acl) # permit tcp host x.1.28.2 eq bgp host x.1.28.8\nSW1(config-acl) # permit pim host x.1.28.2 host x.1.28.8\n…\n…\n…\nSW1(config-acl)# deny ip any any",
          "group_id": "V-221142",
